# The two-star reason: why the dice shape is quicker than counting, which is what subitising is.
item k.quick-or-count v=1 stars=2 skills=[counting.subitising, reasoning.explain] {
  title "Why is a dice quick to read?"

  scene 30x16 {
    dice d faces=[5, 6] at=canvas(1, 1)
    text q "Ada knows the dice show five and six without counting. How?" narrate width=28 below=d gap=1
    choice pick options=["The dots make a shape she knows.", "She guessed."] stack=column below=q gap=1
  }

  answer pick="The dots make a shape she knows."
  hint "What shape do five dots make on a dice?"
  hint "Would she know it again on another dice?"
}
